  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The political impasse in Israel continues following the unsuccessful conclusion of negotiations between the Likud party, led by caretaker Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu, and the Yashar party, headed by Gadi Eisenkot. The two groups held a four-hour meeting at a hotel in Herzliya to address potential concessions needed to establish a governing coalition. These discussions followed earlier developments in the Knesset, where an ally of Gadi Eisenkot was elected speaker with support from an Arab legislative bloc. Arab parties, which hold a record 19 seats in the current legislature, have maintained their opposition to Benjamin Netanyahu remaining in power. The ongoing deadlock highlights deep divisions within the Israeli political landscape, as both sides face significant hurdles in securing enough support to form a stable majority government in the current parliamentary environment.",
